her yourself."},{"t":98.6,"txt":"Put them together yourself is the"},{"t":100.3,"txt":"defining characteristic of IKEA"},{"t":102.1,"txt":"furniture. In Western culture, this is a"},{"t":105,"txt":"universal reference to the frustration"},{"t":106.9,"txt":"and effort of assembling flatpack"},{"t":109,"txt":"furniture to save money."},{"t":111.6,"txt":"Our relationship is like an IKEA desk. I"},{"t":114.2,"txt":"had to put it together myself. A"},{"t":116.6,"txt":"humorous metaphor for doing all the work"},{"t":118.3,"txt":"in a situation."},{"t":123,"txt":">> Look, Rachel, this is poker. I play to"},{"t":125.4,"txt":"win. All right. In order"},{"t":126.5,"txt":">> play to win. Play to win is a mindset"},{"t":129.8,"txt":"where victory is the only acceptable"},{"t":131.5,"txt":"outcome. It suggests being ruthless and"},{"t":133.8,"txt":"not holding back. It's the opposite of"},{"t":135.9,"txt":"playing just for fun."},{"t":138.5,"txt":"In this business, you have to play to"},{"t":140.2,"txt":"win or you'll be eaten alive. It"},{"t":143,"txt":"emphasizes a competitive, ruthless"},{"t":145,"txt":"approach to business."},{"t":151.4,"txt":">> Before work tomorrow,"},{"t":152.9,"txt":">> rage, we got to settle."},{"t":154.6,"txt":">> Settle what?"},{"t":157,"txt":">> The Jamestown colony of Virginia."},{"t":159.2,"txt":"[laughter]"},{"t":161.4,"txt":"You see, King George is giving us the"},{"t":163,"txt":"land."},{"t":167.2,"txt":"The game, Rachel, the game. You owe us"},{"t":169.5,"txt":"money for the game. Mr."},{"t":175.4,"txt":"Ra, we got to settle."},{"t":177.5,"txt":">> Settle."},{"t":179.3,"txt":"Settle here is a brilliant double"},{"t":181,"txt":"entandra. In finance, it means to pay a"},{"t":183.7,"txt":"debt. In history, it means to colonize"},{"t":186.6,"txt":"land. Ross uses the first meaning, but"},{"t":189.1,"txt":"Rachel jokingly switches to the second."},{"t":192.3,"txt":"Let's settle the bill before we leave"},{"t":193.8,"txt":"the restaurant. It means to pay what is"},{"t":196.4,"txt":"owed."},{"t":197.8,"txt":"The pioneers arrived to settle the"},{"t":199.4,"txt":"valley in 1850."},{"t":201.4,"txt":"It means to establish a community in a"},{"t":203.5,"txt":"new place."},{"t":207.4,"txt":">> The Jamestown colony of Virginia."},{"t":209.6,"txt":"[laughter]"},{"t":211.7,"txt":">> The game. Rachel. The game. You owe us"},{"t":213.9,"txt":"money for the game."},{"t":215,"txt":">> Oh,"},{"t":220.6,"txt":"God. You should have seen him. Read him"},{"t":222.7,"txt":"and wait. And then he did."},{"t":227.1,"txt":"Well, now how come you guys have never"},{"t":229.6,"txt":"played poker with us?"},{"t":231,"txt":">> Yeah. What is that? Like some kind of"},{"t":232.6,"txt":"guy thing? Like some kind of sexist,"},{"t":237.8,"txt":">> right?"},{"t":240.4,"txt":"You should have seen him. Read them and"},{"t":242.6,"txt":"weep."},{"t":243.8,"txt":">> Read them and weep."},{"t":246.1,"txt":"Read them and weep is a classic arrogant"},{"t":248.6,"txt":"phrase used when revealing a winning"},{"t":250.4,"txt":"hand in poker. It means look at my"},{"t":253.1,"txt":"victory and cry because you lost. Use it"},{"t":256.1,"txt":"when you are absolutely certain you have"},{"t":257.9,"txt":"beaten your opponent."},{"t":260.1,"txt":"I put my final test score on the table"},{"t":261.8,"txt":"and said, \"Read them and weep, mom.\" It"},{"t":264.8,"txt":"playfully announces a surprising"},{"t":266.6,"txt":"success."},{"t":269.4,"txt":">> Never played poker with us."},{"t":271,"txt":">> Yeah. What is that? Like some kind of"},{"t":272.6,"txt":"guy thing? Like some kind of second"},{"t":274.4,"txt":">> guy thing?"},{"t":276.2,"txt":"Guy thing refers to activities or"},{"t":277.9,"txt":"behaviors stereotypically associated"},{"t":280.2,"txt":"with men. often implying women wouldn't"},{"t":282.4,"txt":"understand or enjoy them. It's often"},{"t":284.5,"txt":"used dismissively."},{"t":286.7,"txt":"They refuse to ask for directions. It's"},{"t":288.6,"t